Fix Lua bit.tohex stack overflow on INT32_MIN (CVE-2024-31449)

bit.tohex(x, n) negates a negative digit count n to select uppercase
output. When n is INT32_MIN the negation overflows and stays negative,
so the (size_t)n cast passed to lua_pushlstring reads far past the
8-byte stack buffer. Clamp INT32_MIN to INT32_MIN+1 before negating.

Tracker: CVE-2024-31449
Upstream patch: https://github.com/redis/redis/commit/1f7c148be2cbacf7d50aa461c58b871e87cc5ed9
Adaptation: deps/lua/src/lua_bit.c is byte-identical to Redis 6.2 in KeyDB v6.3.4, so the C hunk applies verbatim. The tests/unit/scripting.tcl hunk was re-anchored: KeyDB (forked from Redis 6.2.6) lacks the "Attempt to modify a readonly table" test used as upstream context, so the new test is inserted before "Test an example script DECR_IF_GT" using the "Globals protection setting an undeclared global" test as context.

diff --git a/deps/lua/src/lua_bit.c b/deps/lua/src/lua_bit.c
--- a/deps/lua/src/lua_bit.c
+++ b/deps/lua/src/lua_bit.c
@@ -131,6 +131,7 @@ static int bit_tohex(lua_State *L)
   const char *hexdigits = "0123456789abcdef";
   char buf[8];
   int i;
+  if (n == INT32_MIN) n = INT32_MIN+1;
   if (n < 0) { n = -n; hexdigits = "0123456789ABCDEF"; }
   if (n > 8) n = 8;
   for (i = (int)n; --i >= 0; ) { buf[i] = hexdigits[b & 15]; b >>= 4; }
diff --git a/tests/unit/scripting.tcl b/tests/unit/scripting.tcl
--- a/tests/unit/scripting.tcl
+++ b/tests/unit/scripting.tcl
@@ -405,6 +405,12 @@ start_server {tags {"scripting"}} {
         set e
     } {*ERR*attempted to create global*}
 
+    test {lua bit.tohex bug} {
+        set res [r eval {return bit.tohex(65535, -2147483648)} 0]
+        r ping
+        set res
+    } {0000FFFF}
+
